## LINQ Learning Roadmap

### Phase 1: Foundation (Step 0)

1. Waht is LINQ?
It standards for Language integrated Query its name indicates that 
 Language--> C# 
 integrated --> Built-in (Language ke andar built-in)
 Query --> Query for Data search/sorting or filter, 

Linq is the features of C# which is used to searching, sorting,filtering, Grouping and transforming the data.
Example: Suppose we have 10000 employees and we have to show only IT employees which has salary 60000 in asc/desc order.

Earlier Developer was doing manual loop like :
List<int> list = new List<int>(){
    10,20,30,40,50
}
foreach(var d in list)
{
 if(d>25)
 Console.WriteLine(d);
}
But in case of LINQ we can do it in one line like 
var d= list.Where(x=>x>25);

Note: we can apply LINQ on array, List, Hashset, Dictionary,XML, Database,EntityFramework & Datatable,
Stack, Queue,LinkedList.

2. IEnumerable: IEnumerable is an interface which provides the one-one element read capability to the any 
collections. It provides only read & iterations capability we can't modify 
IEnumerable<int> nums = new List<int>(){10,20,30,40}

    Note: 
    1. Once you implemented IEnumerable then it provides capability to foreach to iterating the loop we can read
    2. All the Methods of Linq (where(),select(),orde etc.) runs on IEnumerable 

    Doubts: If IEnumerable is there then whats the use of it while IEnumerable is also providing read and iterating
    the loop and collections also can do then why IEnumerable?
    Ans: IEnumerable doesn't store the the data it can only read or iterate the data, To store the data we need 
    collections so thats why we can't use IEnumerable instead of collections.
    3. Foreach & LINQ needs IEnumerable to read the collections data
    4. Whenever you are using foreach loop then compiler don't know foreach loop using which collections
    so it needs a way to read the data one-one so those ways provides IEnumerable.
    5. Foreach don't know which the internal implementation of List it only Knows the IEnumerable contract.
    6. For loop its is an index based so it doesn't need IEnumerable but in case of foreach its need.


--IEnumerable doesn't store the data itself it takes the data from any datasource and datasource may anything like
List, Dictionary,HashSet,Array,XML,File, Yield return, Database.

Example 1: List
List<int> list = new List<int>()
{
    10,20,30,40,50
};
IEnumerable<int> nums = list;

1. Now data are in the list but IEnumerable is pointing to the list 
2. When Foreach loop is running then internally flow is like 

foreach(var item in list)
{
    Console.WriteLine(item);
}

At running time Compiler Convert above code into below code :
IEnumerator<int> enumerator = list.GetEnumerator();

while(enumerator.MoveNext())
{
    int item = enumerator.Current;
    Console.WriteLine(item);
}


IEnumerable completely works on RAM so when where we have to work on samll data then we use it .
Else whever we have to work on huge data like 2M comming from SQL server then we use IQueryable.



